    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Once dubbed the tiniest town in Iowa, Asbury sits in Section 20 of Dubuque Township.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityofasbury.com/about_asbury/asbury_history"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1868, a one-room tavern operated by Kelly served Asbury’s early residents.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityofasbury.com/about_asbury/asbury_history"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1933, Asbury incorporated after the Twenty‑first Amendment ended prohibition, allowing the town to legally sell alcohol.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
